@format 1
@id relay.deliver-output
@title Deliver completed output
@area 6. Relay and routing
@entry input
@summary Deliver a completed output, optionally drain its source tab, and show how an inactive source tab can retain flow sections after its file and viewer are removed.
@section II. Functionality
@flow TB
@related processing.complete, queue.clear-tabs, relay.receive-tab
@tag relay
@tag delivery

@alias courier = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainArea.LCourier
@alias list = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PList
@alias group = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PGroup
@alias surface = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainArea.PTabSurface
@alias viewer = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PViewer
@alias window = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainWindow.PWindow
@alias flow = Cadroue.UIShell.PFlow.PFlow

[input] Schedule change after completion <input>
- Scan done work owned by this process for undelivered relay targets @ courier.LCourierDispatch(...)
> target

[target] Resolve delivery target <decision>
? "Finish target" > finish
? "Output exists and destination tab is available" > add
? "Output or destination is unavailable" > skipped

[finish] Finish relay chain <process>
- Record chain completion and force source removal @ courier.LCourierOutputAdd(...)
> drain

[add] Add output to destination <process>
- Add the output path to the destination list with its batch cohort @ list.PListPathsAdd(...)
> drain

[drain] Should source inputs be removed? <decision>
- Apply the force flag, relay-empty preference, source-tab identity, and source-tab availability checks @ courier.LCourierSourceRemove(...)
? "Source removal is disabled or impossible" > arrive
? "Source removal proceeds" > remove

[remove] Remove source containers <process>
- Remove the delivered source and merge-source paths from the source list @ list.PListPathsRemove(...)
- Remove matching paths from the source group container @ group.PGroupPathsRemove(...)
- Close the source viewer when the removed list entry is its loaded media @ surface.PTabViewerAttach(...)
- Raise an empty-media notification after the viewer closes @ viewer.PViewerMediaClose(...)
> active

[active] Is the source workspace active? <decision>
- The window media handler is attached only to the active viewer @ window.PWindowWorkspaceAttach(...)
? "Source viewer is active" > flow-clear
? "Source viewer is inactive" > retained

[flow-clear] Clear active source flow <process>
- Receive the empty-media notification and clear the active flow state @ window.PWindowMediaHandle(...)
- Remove its source, spool, sections, keyframes, and waveform state @ flow.PFlowClear(...)
> arrive

[retained] Inactive source flow remains <error>
- Leave the inactive source flow unchanged because no window media handler is subscribed to that viewer @ window.PWindowWorkspaceDetach(...)
> arrive

[arrive] Continue downstream relay <process>
- Invoke automatic downstream action when enabled @ courier.LCourierArrive(...)
> result

[skipped] Delivery skipped <error>
- Record the missing output or destination @ courier.LCourierOutputAdd(...)
= The completed work remains done but is not delivered.

[result] Delivery complete <output>
= The destination receives the output, while an inactive drained source tab can still display sections belonging to the removed media.
